Functieomschrijving

Responsibilities

You will work on improving the quality and efficiency of assembly processes in a high-tech mechatronic manufacturing environment. Your responsibilities include:

Initiating and implementing technical and quality improvement plans;
Monitoring product quality and material availability for assembly;
Investigating and resolving internal quality issues and non-conformities;
Analysing deviations and identifying the root cause of problems;
Developing and implementing structural corrective actions;
Preparing quality reports and improvement documentation;
Working closely with production, engineering and quality teams;
Coaching and supporting production teams in solving quality problems;
Improving processes to prevent recurring quality issues;
Contributing to a culture of continuous improvement and quality awareness.

You won't spend your entire day behind a desk. You will regularly be on the production floor, working directly with the people and processes involved.

Functie-eisen

You are a technically minded professional who can combine hands-on problem solving with analytical thinking. You have:

A completed Bachelor's degree (HBO) in a technical field, such as Mechanical Engineering, Mechatronics or Industrial Engineering;
Experience with assembly processes in a mechatronic manufacturing environment;
Experience with process control and quality systems;
Knowledge of Process FMEA (PFMEA) and Control Plans;
Knowledge of industrial production standards and manufacturing processes;
Strong analytical and problem-solving skills;
Excellent communication skills;
A structured and proactive approach;
The ability to coach and motivate colleagues on the production floor.

Experience with Lean Manufacturing, 5S, quality management systems and logistics processes is a strong advantage.

